tentials resulting from the simulated eye movements for horizontal saccade (a) and blinking (b).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.001"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>The <inline-formula><mml:math id="M212"><mml:mrow><mml:mtext>asd</mml:mtext></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula> as a function of the correlation threshold <inline-formula><mml:math id="M213"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003d1;</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula> and of the window length <inline-formula><mml:math id="M214"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>T</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>An example of a simulated dataset with blinks at an average of 5&#x02009;dB above the background EEG level (SNR &#x02212;5&#x02009;dB).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.003"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>The cleaned simulation dataset.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.004"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>The first extracted source as estimated by JADE, pSVD, and JSSE. The ordening by JADE was done with descending kurtosis.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.005"/></fig><fig id="fig6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Values of SDR (a), SAR (b), and SIR (c) as a function of the SNR levels.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.006"/></fig><fig id="fig7" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>An example fragment of blinking artefacts. The blinks are clearly visible at seconds 1, 3, and 7.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.007"/></fig><fig id="fig8" position="float"><label>Figure 8</label><caption><p>The results after having subjected the blink fragment of <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig7">Figure 7</xref> to JSSE.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.008"/></fig><fig id="fig9" position="float"><label>Figure 9</label><caption><p>An example fragment of saccades. The saccades are clearly visible at seconds 1, 5, and 8.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.009"/></fig><fig id="fig10" position="float"><label>Figure 10</label><caption><p>The results after having subjected the saccade fragment of <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig9">Figure 9</xref> to JSSE.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.010"/></fig><fig id="fig11" position="float"><label>Figure 11</label><caption><p>The pSVD profile associated with the blink fragment of <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig7">Figure 7</xref>. The bars denote the number of deflations that occurred for each 8 sample window (with a maximum of 4 occurrences, see text).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.011"/></fig><fig id="fig12" position="float"><label>Figure 12</label><caption><p>The spectrum of the subspace angles as obtained by the blink frame of <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig7">Figure 7</xref>. The dashed horizontal line denotes the threshold level of 0.9.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.012"/></fig><fig id="fig13" position="float"><label>Figure 13</label><caption><p>The topography of the first source of JADE (a) and an estimation of the JSSE topography, based on the reconstruction in (<xref ref-type="disp-formula" rid="eq2.8">9</xref>) (b).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-75079.013"/></fig><table-wrap id="tab1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>The template library composed of column vectors (here transposed and limited to their core information) as used in <xref ref-type="statement" rid="cri1">Criterion 1</xref>.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Fp1</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Fp2</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Fpz</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">F7</th><t